.TH APP-MEMORY-BAR-MIGRATE 1 "November 2026" "App Memory Bar" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
app-memory-bar-migrate \- migrate a per-user App Memory Bar installation to the packaged system installation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B app-memory-bar-migrate
.RB [ --status | --migrate | --automatic ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B app-memory-bar-migrate
backs up an App Memory Bar plasmoid installed below the current user's XDG data directory and a per-user
.B app-memory-bar.service
unit that would otherwise shadow the files installed by the Debian package.
.PP
Backups are stored below
.BR $XDG_STATE_HOME/app-memory-bar/migration-backup/
(or
.BR ~/.local/state/app-memory-bar/migration-backup/
when XDG_STATE_HOME is unset). Plasma widget configuration and
.B ~/.config/app-memory-bar/
are not removed.
.PP
The command must be run as the desktop user, not as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --status
Print the detected system and local installation state as JSON.
.TP
.B --migrate
Run the migration immediately and restart the packaged user backend.
.TP
.B --automatic
Non-interactive mode used by the packaged systemd user migration service. The backend start is queued without waiting for it.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/plasma/plasmoids/cz.pitriss.appmemorybar/
Default location of a legacy per-user plasmoid installation.
.TP
.B ~/.config/systemd/user/app-memory-bar.service
Per-user unit that shadows the packaged unit and is backed up during migration.
.TP
.B ~/.local/state/app-memory-bar/migration-v1.json
Migration state marker when XDG_STATE_HOME is unset.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1)
